===========================================================
 GAMECLIP - HOW TO MAKE A VIDEO
===========================================================

THE THREE STEPS
---------------
1. Drop the recording in  raw/
2. Watch it and mark the good moments in a clips file  (MANUAL, by design)
3. Run one command

Everything after step 2 is automatic.


THE COMMAND
-----------
  python main.py <recording> <clips file> --series <preset> --name <folder>

Real examples:

  python main.py raw/ghost_reocon.mkv clips_ghost.txt --series vehicle_test --name ghost_04

  python main.py raw/session01.mkv clips.txt --series default --name farcry_07

Output lands in  output/<date>_<name>/  containing:
  video.mp4        the finished short
  thumbnail.png    auto-picked representative frame
  seo.txt          title, description, hashtags - built from YOUR clips file
  clips_used.txt   what was used, in final order, with hook scores


THE CLIPS FILE - the only part you write
----------------------------------------
  # game:  Ghost Recon Wildlands
  # title: CHOPPER GUNRUN OVER BOLIVIA

  01:52   02:05   driving     "Bolivian Highway Carnage!"
  42:32   42:41   driving     "Ultimate Chopper Ambush"
  43:25   43:53   explosion   "Wiping Out the Convoy"

  START  END  LABEL  "optional caption"

  - "# game:" picks the logo from assets/logos/<slug>.png and tells the
    metadata AI which game it is looking at. "Far Cry 5" looks for
    far_cry_5.png. Missing logo = skipped with a log line, never an error.
  - Timestamps take 4:32 or 1:04:32
  - "# title:" is the hook burned across the top. REQUIRED in practice -
    without it the render warns, because nothing else can describe your
    footage. The pipeline cannot see the video.
  - The quoted caption shows in the top zone for that clip only
  - Labels lowercase: DRIVING and driving become two different hashtags
  - Aim for 4-6 clips of 8-12s. One long clip is the weakest possible
    short, and hook detection needs more than one clip to do anything.


THE OPTIONS
-----------
--series   Controls how the video LOOKS. Nothing else. It says nothing
           about what is in the footage, so running vehicle_test on a
           gunfight for its grade and music is perfectly fine.

           default        tense music, fade,      normal grade
           vehicle_test   hype music,  fast fade, punchy saturated grade
           stealth        quiet tense, fadeblack, cold desaturated grade
                          *** also uses the facecam_top layout, which is
                              NOT yet proven on real footage - see below

--name     Output folder name. Skip it and you get a timestamped one.

--title    Same as "# title:" in the clips file, and overrides it.
           Use the clips file normally - the title belongs with the
           timestamps that describe the same video.

--game     Overrides the "# game:" line for this run.

--keep-work  Keeps the intermediate clips in .work/ so you can inspect
             them when something looks wrong.


WHAT HAPPENS AUTOMATICALLY
--------------------------
  cut       each clip cut, graded, converted to 9:16, reaction cam added
            - all in ONE encode per clip
  hook      every clip scored on motion + loudness
  cold open the strongest clip's last 2.5s is teased at the very start,
            and that clip STILL plays in full in its own place
  join      clips joined with the series transition
  audio     music picked from assets/music/<mood>/, ducked under gameplay
  export    hook title at the start AND again over the closing seconds,
            per-clip captions in between, thumbnail, seo.txt


THE FRAME
---------
  0    -> 257    hook title / captions
  257  -> 1139   gameplay
  1155 -> 1623   your reaction cam
  1640 -> 1920   NOTHING - YouTube and Instagram draw their own UI here

Tune in config.py: GAMEPLAY_HEIGHT, TEXT_ZONE_SHARE, SAFE_BOTTOM,
REACTION_HEIGHT, REACTION_ZOOM, COLD_OPEN_SECONDS, HOOK_OUTRO_SECONDS.


GAME LOGOS
----------
Put transparent PNGs in assets/logos/, named after the game in lowercase
with underscores:

  assets/logos/far_cry_5.png
  assets/logos/ghost_recon_wildlands.png

They appear under the hook title for the first 3 seconds of the video,
and bottom centre on the thumbnail. Any width works - both are scaled
to a fixed fraction of the frame (LOGO_VIDEO_WIDTH, LOGO_THUMBNAIL_WIDTH).


KNOWN GAPS
----------
- assets/logos/ is empty, so no game logo is drawn yet.
- assets/overlays/ is empty, so hook text always uses drawtext. Drop in
  <title-slug>.png or <series>.png to use a real graphic instead.
- Only reactions_white_tshirt.mp4 is usable. reactions_black_tshirt.mp4
  is 10s against a 20s segment table, so it is skipped every run and
  there is no costume variety yet.
- REACTION_MATCH_LABELS is False: every clip gets the same idle segment
  regardless of its label.
- Your reaction audio is dropped. REACTION_MUTE is a dead flag.
- stealth's facecam_top layout has never been rendered with the real
  landscape reaction video. Try it on a throwaway --name first.
